---Internal Transfer
---
---Submit a signed internal ledger transfer between two exchange accounts.
---Sign with the source account owner or a non-expired trading key registered
---to the source account. Trading-key signatures require both accounts to
---belong to the same nonzero, exchange-managed account group. Owner signatures
---remain valid regardless of group membership.
---
---Expired trading keys receive `proxy_expired`; other authorization failures
---receive `signer_does_not_match_account`. An unknown destination receives 400
---`destination account not found`.
---
---A 503 does not prove that the transfer was not submitted. Retry with backoff,
---honoring `Retry-After` when present, and resend the exact original signed
---request. Do not create a fresh signature, salt, or timestamp for the retry: it
---would identify a separate transfer. A `signature_already_used` rejection does
---not confirm whether the original transfer completed.
---
---`POST /v1/account/internal-transfer`
---@param input polymarket.perps.TransferInternalRequest
---@return polymarket.perps.InternalTransferAccepted? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:transfer_internal(input) end

---Update your builder display name
---
---Sign with the owner wallet of an existing registered Perps builder using
---the standard signed-operation format: op.type is updateBuilder and
---op.args contains only name. No Admin credentials or trading proxy are needed.
---The signer determines the account; no address or version parameter is accepted.
---Names are trimmed and must contain 1 to 100 Unicode characters without control characters.
---
---Name edits use last-write-wins. Repeating the saved name succeeds.
---Disabled builders can edit their name. This operation does not change
---registration, enablement, the platform admission switch, approvals or fees.
---
---`PATCH /v1/account/builder`
---@param input polymarket.perps.UpdateBuilderRequest
---@return polymarket.perps.UpdateBuilderResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_builder(input) end

---Update Leverage
---
---Update leverage for an instrument.
---
---Each setting resolves independently: explicit per-instrument setting, then
---exchange-managed account-group default, then instrument maximum leverage and
---isolated margin. Group leverage is capped at the instrument maximum; a group
---cross default resolves to isolated on isolated-only instruments. Group defaults
---apply to new listings and never overwrite explicit settings.
---This operation sets both settings explicitly; GET /v1/account/config reports
---resolved values. Submit the current resolved pair to preserve it against later
---group changes. Leverage bounds and BLP locks also apply to unchanged values.
---Set your preferred leverage and margin mode after listing and before placing
---your first order. An unknown instrument ID (never listed) is rejected with
---`instrument_not_found`; a disabled instrument is not rejected merely because
---it is disabled.
---
---Margin mode can change only when the account has no position and no open
---orders in that instrument, including orders awaiting risk approval or execution.
---Close the position and cancel all orders before switching between isolated
---and cross margin. A position blocks a mode change with `position_exists`;
---open orders block it with `open_orders_exist`. Leverage changes within the
---same mode remain subject to leverage limits and margin checks. Leverage must
---be positive (`lev: 0` returns 400); exceeding the instrument maximum returns
---`invalid_leverage`. BLP-subscribed instruments reject leverage or mode updates
---with `blp_leverage_locked`; unsubscribe before changing the configuration.
---
---Requires proxy signature, see [proxy signing](/http/signing#2-proxy-signing).
---
---`PATCH /v1/trade/leverage`
---@param input polymarket.perps.UpdateLeverageRequest
---@return polymarket.perps.LeverageResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_leverage(input) end

---Update Leverage for Multiple Instruments
---
---Update leverage for up to 100 unique instruments. Updates are processed
---sequentially and are not atomic. If only some responses arrive before the
---gateway deadline, missing item results use `internal_error`; whether those
---updates applied is unknown. If no responses arrive, the request returns
---503 — retryable, since each update is an idempotent leverage/margin-type
---set that converges to the same value whether or not the original attempt
